example.paragraph:
The coefficients of this linear combination are precisely the entries in the coordinate vector. Thus $\left\lbrack \left\{ y_{k} \right\} \right\rbrack_{B_{2}} = \,\,\begin{bmatrix}
      2 \\
      3 \\
      {- 1}
      \end{bmatrix}$

statement.paragraph:
Let $W = \left\{ \left. \left\{ x_{k} \right\}\  \right|\ x_{k} = \left\{ \begin{array}{ll}
      0 & {\text{if~}k\text{~is~a~multiple~of~2}} \\
      r & {\text{if~}k\text{~is~not~a~multiple~of~2}}
      \end{array} \text{where~}r\text{~can~be~any~real~number} \right. \right\}$. A typical signal in $W$ looks like $$\begin{matrix}
      (\ldots,\,r,\,0,\,r,\,0,\,r,\,0,\,r,\,\ldots) \\
       \uparrow \\
      {k = 0}
      \end{matrix}$$

Let $W = \left\{ {\left. \left\{ x_{k} \right\}\  \right|\ }x_{k} = \left\{ \begin{array}{ll}
      0 & {\text{if~}k < 0} \\
      r & {\text{if~}k \geq 0}
      \end{array} \text{where~}r\text{~can~be~any~real~number} \right. \right\}.$ A typical signal in $W$ looks like

$$\begin{matrix}
      (\ldots,\,0,\,0,\,0,\,r,\,r,\,r,\,r,\,\ldots) \\
       \uparrow \\
      {k = 0}
      \end{matrix}$$Show that $W$ is a subspace of $\mathbb{S}$.

Let $W = \left\{ {\left. \left\{ x_{k} \right\}\  \right|\ }x_{k} = \begin{cases}
      0 & {\text{if~}k\text{~is~a~multiple~of~2}} \\
      r_{k} & {\text{if~}k\text{~is~not~a~multiple~of~2}}
      \end{cases} \right.$ where each $r_{k}$ can be any real number}. A typical signal in $W$ looks like $$\begin{matrix}
      \left( \ldots,\,r_{- 3},\,0,\,r_{- 1},\,0,\,r_{1},\,0,\,r_{3},\,\ldots \right) \\
       \uparrow \\
      {k = 0}
      \end{matrix}$$

Let $W = \left\{ \left. \left\{ x_{k} \right\}\  \right|\ x_{k} = \left\{ \begin{array}{ll}
      0 & {\text{if~}k < 0} \\
      r_{k} & {\text{if~}k \geq 0}
      \end{array} \text{where~each~}r_{k}\text{~can~be~any~real~number} \right. \right\}$. A typical signal in $W$ looks like$$\begin{matrix}
      \left( \ldots,\,0,\,0,0,\,r_{0},\,r_{1},\,r_{2},\,r_{3},\,\ldots \right) \\
      \left. \mspace{-4mu}\mspace{-4mu}\mspace{-4mu}\uparrow \right. \\
      {\mspace{-4mu}\mspace{-4mu}\mspace{-4mu} k = 0}
      \end{matrix}$$
